Handling All Negative Numbers

Consider:

[-5, -2, -8, -1]

The maximum subarray is:

[-1]

So the answer is:

-1

That is why we initialize:

current_sum = arr[0]
max_sum = arr[0]
Time and Space Complexity
Time Complexity:  O(n)
Space Complexity: O(1)

We go through the array only once and use only a few variables.

Key Takeaways
Kadane's Algorithm finds the maximum sum of a contiguous subarray.
At each element, choose between starting fresh or continuing the previous subarray.
Main formula:
current_sum = max(current_element, current_sum + current_element)
Update the maximum sum at every step.
Time complexity is O(n).
Space complexity is O(1).
